# Home-Tutor.lk

## Development Errors & Solutions

During the development of the Home-Tutor.lk web application, several technical issues were identified during coding, testing, and Git-based collaboration. The following section describes the main issues and the solutions applied.

---

### 01. Git Merge Conflict

**Problem:**
A merge conflict occurred when changes from different team members were merged into the same branch.

**Cause:**
Multiple team members had modified the same file or the same section of a file.

**Solution Implemented:**
The conflicting sections were reviewed manually. The required code was kept, unnecessary conflict markers were removed, and the file was tested before committing the changes.

**Result:**
The branches were successfully merged without losing the required changes.

**Status:** ✅ Resolved

---

### 02. CSS File Not Loading

**Problem:**
Some pages were displayed without the expected styling.

**Cause:**
The CSS file path specified in the HTML `<link>` element was incorrect.

**Solution Implemented:**
The folder structure and CSS file path were checked and the `<link>` element was corrected.

**Result:**
The CSS file loaded correctly and the page displayed the expected styles.

**Status:** ✅ Resolved

---

### 03. JavaScript Function Not Working

**Problem:**
A button did not perform the expected action when clicked.

**Cause:**
The JavaScript code was referring to an incorrect HTML element ID.

**Solution Implemented:**
The HTML element ID and the JavaScript selector were compared and corrected so that both matched.

**Result:**
The button successfully triggered the required JavaScript function.

**Status:** ✅ Resolved

---

### 04. Incorrect Image/File Path

**Problem:**
Images or other resources were not displayed correctly on the webpage.

**Cause:**
The file path used in the HTML code did not match the actual project folder structure.

**Solution Implemented:**
The location of the required files was checked and the relative paths were corrected.

**Result:**
The required images and resources were displayed correctly.

**Status:** ✅ Resolved

---

### 05. Responsive Design Issue

**Problem:**
Some webpage elements did not display correctly on smaller screen sizes.

**Cause:**
Certain elements used fixed dimensions that were not suitable for different screen sizes.

**Solution Implemented:**
Responsive CSS techniques and media queries were added to adjust the layout for different screen widths.

**Result:**
The webpage became more suitable for desktop, tablet, and mobile screen sizes.

**Status:** ✅ Resolved

---

### 06. Form Validation Issue

**Problem:**
Users could submit a form without entering some required information.

**Cause:**
Required fields and validation rules were not properly implemented.

**Solution Implemented:**
HTML validation attributes and JavaScript validation checks were added to the relevant form fields.

**Result:**
Users are now prompted to enter the required information before submitting the form.

**Status:** ✅ Resolved

---

### 07. Git Pull / Push Issue

**Problem:**
Changes could not be pushed or pulled correctly from the remote GitHub repository.

**Cause:**
The local branch and remote repository were not synchronized correctly.

**Solution Implemented:**
The current branch and remote repository status were checked. The latest changes were pulled, conflicts were resolved where necessary, and the changes were committed and pushed again.

**Result:**
The local project and GitHub repository were synchronized successfully.

**Status:** ✅ Resolved

---

